abstract: >-
  For a prime p, a monic A in Z[z][t] of t-degree d with A(z, sum z^(p^n)) congruent to 0 modulo
  p^gamma exists if and only if p^gamma divides d!, which proves Conjecture 4 of Kauers,
  Krattenthaler and Mueller for every prime. The least number of divisor levels for the Moebius
  function modulo p^k is S(p^k) - 1, S the Kempner function; the bound holds for every Dirichlet
  inverse over every commutative ring, and a depth-flag formula gives the exact count for units of
  Z_p[[x_1, ..., x_n]] and of the Dirichlet ring over Z and Z_p. Every theorem of the accompanying
  preprint is machine-checked in Lean 4. Prepared with Claude (Anthropic). No external human referee
  has reviewed this work.
keywords:
  - Kempner function
  - Moebius function
